{
 "about": "The live rule monitor's pre-registration (scripts/rule_monitor.py), 2026-10-21; the statistics redone 2026-11-09. One test, decide(), for every rule that bets. A Predictions pick rule or segment (scripts/games_picks.py) is judged by game day, each day's evidence divided by 1 + (n - 1) rho, rho the within-slate correlation of close value on the rule's held-out picks (games_picks_rules.json clvIcc). With minN+ bets judged by the close since its clock started it stops on any of: the one-sided CUSUM around zero (cusum k, h: losing to the close); the CUSUM of the log likelihood ratio of no edge against the edge its stakes assume (cusum hL); the drift test's pause. The last `window` bets' clustered t (se never under the iid one) is shown and stops nothing. A rule with no slate structure (the model monitor's losses) keeps the test against zero: the window's t under the Student cut at the one-sided level `t` stands for, with minDays+ game days, or the per-bet CUSUM. A stopped rule comes back only when it is refit (its X changes, or k moves past 10%), which restarts its clock.",
 "registered": "2026-10-21",
 "window": 300,
 "minN": 50,
 "minDays": 8,
 "t": -1.0,
 "cusum": {
  "k": 0.25,
  "h": 10.0,
  "note": "Around zero: S = max(0, S + sum over the day of (-z - k) / (1 + (n - 1) rho)), z = clvRet / sd; k .25, h 10 as registered Oct 21 (the log likelihood ratio of losing half an sd a bet against the close, at 148:1). Per bet and undeflated, as first run, it stopped a rule earning exactly its stakes' edge 9-52% of the time on the history's own slates; by day and deflated 0-3%. Against the stakes' edge (hL): S = max(0, S - day LLR), the drift test's game-day log likelihood ratio (reference mu1 / 2), stop at hL = ln 99. ln 19 and ln 39 stopped an NFL spread rule at its edge 39% and 21% of the time over 300 bets; ln 99 9%, every other market rule 0-1%. The window test (last 300, clustered t < -1) is no longer a stop: checked at every build from 50 bets, with a clustered se that few game days put under the iid one, it and the per-bet CUSUM stopped a rule at its stakes' edge 15-54% of the time.",
  "hL": 4.595
 },
 "sdDefault": 0.12,
 "weekDays": 7,
 "zFlag": 2.0,
 "drift": {
  "registered": "2026-11-01",
  "A": 19,
  "B": 19,
  "minN": 30,
  "note": "Overfit test for every pick rule from its clock (so every new or refit rule): Wald's SPRT, H1 the rule is worth its held-out backtest's clvRet with its edge over a fair coin x units.TIMING x units.LEAK (the edge its stakes assume), H0 it is worth 0. Game-day LLR deflated by the within-slate correlation of close value on the rule's held-out picks (clvIcc; units' rho is the correlation of results, about 0, and made the LLR up to 2.5x too large). Pause at LLR <= -ln B (a stop, cleared only by a refit), confirm at >= ln A (test retires; the close switch keeps running). A 19 / B 19 as registered Nov 1; the error rates per rule are in `rates`."
 },
